  "setup_history": [
    "First runner config had an invalid environment path; corrected locally. Copied old snapshot was rejected for profile mismatch, so one fresh 2 GiB import ran and saved only the local snapshot. The runner closed normally.",
    "Initial comparison exposed initialization primary recapture across allocator reentry and too-early native rejection of a released old pointer. Both source ordering defects were corrected before qualification.",
    "New fixture corrections retained all input vectors: callback mutations must target the actually selected action container; callback spare-node references require a real spare allocation; duplicate-free contract stops precede simulated reentry. Earlier diagnostic reports are superseded.",
    "The first native failure fixture exhausted only the largest free block, leaving small reusable blocks; a second attempt tried to allocate a zero-size sentinel. Final test exhausts every allocatable free block and asserts actual 24-byte failure.",
    "Packaging found PInitialize already owns event allocation. Duplicate typed mode/timer fields were removed; complete event snapshots and a raw-startup-allocation composed case qualify the actual owner.",
    "Final identity retention stores allocation records outside their payloads, preserving released old/head identities without fixture-held handles or ownership cycles. Final source, all seven mutants and a fresh holdout were rerun."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Queue/admission and cleanup only; no animation stepping, controller or render qualification.",
